      "content": "okay, that's much clearer, thanks. so using `.loc` is better because it's more explicit about whether we are touching the original or a copy. \n\ni'm still a little hung up on that \"safety feature\" part though. if i'm intentionally creating a slice to work on separately, why does pandas feel the need to \"warn\" me at all if it's not an actual error? it feels like it's overreacting to something i'm doing on purpose. is there a specific name for this type of ambiguity in memory management, or is it just a quirk of how pandas handles internal pointers?",
